---
/**
 * The two-layer picture that the whole project rests on.
 *
 * Two cards and the link between them, in flowing markup: it reflows on a
 * phone (the arrow turns downwards), it can be read aloud in order, and it
 * takes the page's own colours. The Jekyll site drew this as ASCII art in a
 * <pre>, which wrapped into nonsense on a phone.
 */
---

<div class="arch">
  <div class="arch-row">
    <section class="arch-node card" aria-labelledby="arch-phone">
      <p class="arch-kicker arch-kicker--always"><span class="dot" style="--accent: var(--helsa-move)"></span>Always · on the iPhone</p>
      <h3 id="arch-phone">The app</h3>
      <p class="arch-flow"><span>HealthKit</span><span>analysis</span><span>what you see</span></p>
      <p class="arch-note">
        HealthKit is the store and the analysis runs on the device. It writes water
        and the journal back to Apple Health. This works fully offline, with no
        server at all.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="arch-link">
      <svg class="arch-arrow" width="40" height="20" viewBox="0 0 40 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
           stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M2 10h34M28 3l8 7-8 7" />
      </svg>
      <p>
        <strong>Optional, opt-in, and you type the URL.</strong>
        Mutual TLS plus a device token.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="arch-node card" aria-labelledby="arch-server">
      <p class="arch-kicker arch-kicker--optional"><span class="dot" style="--accent: var(--helsa-fjord)"></span>Optional · on your machine</p>
      <h3 id="arch-server">The server — this repository</h3>
      <p class="arch-flow">
        <span>Caddy</span><span>API</span><span>RabbitMQ</span><span>worker</span><span>TimescaleDB</span>
      </p>
      <p class="arch-note">
        Long-term history as a second, queryable copy you control, a web dashboard on
        your LAN or VPN that runs the app's rules, exports, and daily summaries for
        Home Assistant.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <p class="arch-caption">
    The phone is the <strong>only writer</strong>. Every other surface — the web
    dashboard, an iPad, Home Assistant — reads from the server. That asymmetry is
    not a preference: HealthKit has no cloud API, so the device holding the data
    is the only thing that can upload it.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .arch-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: stretch;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .arch-node {
    flex: 1 1 300px;
    padding: 28px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .arch-node h3 { font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0; }
  .arch-kicker {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .arch-kicker--always { color: var(--helsa-move-text); }
  .arch-kicker--optional { color: var(--helsa-accent-text); }

  .arch-flow {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px 8px;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--helsa-font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .arch-flow span {
    background: var(--helsa-surface-2);
    border-radius: var(--helsa-radius-pill);
    padding: 3px 10px;
    color: var(--helsa-text);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  /* The arrows are decoration between the stages, so they are generated rather
     than written into the markup where a screen reader would announce them. */
  .arch-flow span + span::before {
    content: '→';
    color: var(--helsa-text-faint);
    margin-inline: -2px 6px;
  }
  .arch-note { margin: 0; color: var(--helsa-text-2); font-size: 15px; }

  .arch-link {
    flex: 0 1 170px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 0 4px;
    color: var(--helsa-text-dim);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .arch-link p { margin: 0; font-size: 13px; }
  .arch-link strong { color: var(--helsa-text); font-weight: 600; display: block; }
  .arch-arrow { color: var(--helsa-text-faint); }

  .arch-caption {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    color: var(--helsa-text-2);
    font-size: 15px;
    max-width: var(--helsa-measure);
  }
  .arch-caption strong { color: var(--helsa-text); }

  /* Stacked: the link sits between the cards and points down. */
  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .arch-link { flex-basis: 100%; flex-direction: row; justify-content: flex-start; text-align: start; padding: 0 8px; }
    .arch-arrow { transform: rotate(90deg); flex: none; }
  }
</style>
